      # Create an API key; the full key (token) is returned only once. Requires a full-access live key; test
      # keys get 403 test_key_restricted.
      #
      # @param params [Hash] the parameters below, also accepted as keyword arguments
      # @option params [String] :name Limits: 1-100 characters (not trimmed) → 422 invalid_parameter "name is
      #   required (max 100 chars)" Required.
      # @option params [String] :permission One of: full_access, sending_access. Default: full_access.
      # @option params [String] :domain_id Restrict sending to one of the account's domains. Only with
      #   sending_access. Limits: 422 "domain_id can only be used with sending_access" / "unknown domain_id"
      # @option params [String] :mode test creates a zap_test_ key (see API keys). One of: live, test.
      #   Default: live.
      # @option params [String] :stream Restrict the key to one message stream. One of: transactional,
      #   broadcast.
      # @option params [String] :expires_at Limits: must be in the future → 422 "expires_at must be in the
      #   future"
      # @option params [Integer] :expires_in_days Alternative to expires_at; when > 0 it overrides expires_at.
      # @param request_options [Hash] :idempotency_key, :headers, :timeout and :max_retries for this call
      # @return [ZapSMTP::Models::CreatedApiKey]
